        {
          "id": "2f3c9777-0d26-3e05-be5c-1344b651f50b",
          "content": {
            "id": "2f3c9777-0d26-3e05-be5c-1344b651f50b",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "CEO of drugmaker GSK to step down by year's end",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "GSK Chief Executive Emma Walmsley, the first woman to lead a major pharmaceutical company, will step down Dec. 31 after more than eight years at the head of the London-based drugmaker.  Walmsley, 56, will be replaced by Luke Miels, currently GSK\u2019s chief commercial officer, the company said in a statement released on Monday.  While GSK achieved a number of strategic successes under Walmsley, including the spinoff of the consumer health care business Haleon, it has disappointed investors.",
